    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec asked to return a `timezone` field on the owner, derived from the locality/region via the fixed table (NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney, VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne, QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane).\n\nI implemented this as small, cohesive units to keep structural impact low:\n\n1. **New `Timezones` util class** (`util/Timezones.java`) \u2014 a self-contained lookup holding the region\u2192IANA table with a single `of(String region)` method (CC 1, WMC_other 0). Adding behaviour here rather than growing an existing class avoids paying the WMC cost of a large surrounding context.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `timezone` string field to the Owner schema next to `locality` (schema data, no method complexity).\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line that reuses the already-computed region (`CustomerCodes.regionOf(owner.getCustomerCode())`) and feeds it to `Timezones.of(...)`, so `timezone` stays consistent with `locality`.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` passes: a Sydney owner (postcode 2000 \u2192 NSW) yields `locality: \"NSW\"` and `timezone: \"Australia/Sydney\"`. `BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests green.",
